<h1>About Regent Summer Camp</h1>
<p>The Regent Summer Camp (RSC) program brings middle- and high-school students to the Regent University campus for a week of hands-on STEM learning. Students work alongside faculty and peer mentors on small-team projects spanning robotics, biology, chemistry, computer science, and engineering design.</p>

<h2>This Registration System</h2>
<p>This site replaces the spreadsheet-and-email workflow that the program coordinators used in previous years. It was built as a CSCI 450 Software Engineering capstone project by:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Spencer Kotrosa &mdash; Backend Lead &amp; Project Manager</li>
  <li>Steven Copeland &mdash; Frontend Developer</li>
  <li>Ethan Dickinson &mdash; User Stories &amp; Application Logic</li>
  <li>Jaden Abbott &mdash; Frontend Developer &amp; Documentation</li>
  <li>Luke Lacy &mdash; Testing &amp; User Guides</li>
</ul>

<h2>What it does</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Lets parents create an account and add one or more campers.</li>
  <li>Automatically enrolls campers when capacity is available, or places them on a waitlist when it isn&rsquo;t.</li>
  <li>Sends confirmation emails for every enrollment, waitlist placement, withdrawal, and waitlist promotion.</li>
  <li>Promotes the next family on the waitlist the instant a spot opens up &mdash; no manual intervention needed.</li>
  <li>Gives administrators a dashboard for managing camps, viewing rosters, and auditing the email log.</li>
</ul>
